      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the bug described here was already fixed by aosp/4368057: `vma_pfnmap_phys()` builds the address with `PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL` and adds the slice. For the `generic_access_phys()` users in GKI (UIO and PCI sysfs resources; `/dev/mem` is off), the PTEs come from `remap_pfn_range()` at `vm_start`, whose slices follow `vma_slice_offset()` since aosp/4368055, so the old helper already gave the mapped address there.\n\nAs far as I can see, what this patch changes is where the slice comes from: the PTE rather than the VMA geometry. That matters when a driver whose VMAs use `generic_access_phys()` maps a slice that doesn\u0027t follow `vma_slice_offset()`, e.g. with `p3s_remap_pfn_slice()` or through the physical-slice path that aosp/4368009 adds to `vm_iomap_memory()`. `/proc/\u003cpid\u003e/mem` and ptrace would then access the wrong 4KB of the page.\n\nCould you describe that case in the message instead? The change itself looks right to me, and native VMAs are unchanged.",
