      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could you keep a kernel-doc block here, as the other helpers in this header have, and as the `vma_pfnmap_phys()` block it replaces had? It\u0027s also the place to say that the helper reads `args-\u003eptep`, which `struct follow_pfnmap_args` lists as internal, so it must be called between `follow_pfnmap_start()` and `follow_pfnmap_end()`. Something like:\n\n```\n/*\n * p3s_pfnmap_phys - Physical address that a PFN mapping maps\n * @args: Lookup made by follow_pfnmap_start(), not yet ended\n *\n * A PTE of a 4KB VMA maps one 4KB slice of kernel page @args-\u003epfn, and\n * p3s_remap_pfn_slice() can map a slice that vma_slice_offset() would\n * not give its address, so take the slice from the PTE. Call this\n * before follow_pfnmap_end(), while the PTE is mapped and locked.\n */\n```",
