      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would it be OK to drop this `#ifdef`? It would be the first config block in `mm/p3s/pgtable.h`, and it sits inside a function. As far as I can see it isn\u0027t needed: `vma_is_p3s_4k()` is always false without P3S, and `\u003clinux/p3s.h\u003e` defines `__pte_to_phys()` for other architectures, next to the `pte_advance_phys()` fallback that `vma_pte_add_slice()` above already uses without a guard. So the helper can be unconditional:\n\n```\n\tresource_size_t phys \u003d (resource_size_t)args-\u003epfn \u003c\u003c PAGE_SHIFT_KERNEL;\n\n\tif (vma_is_p3s_4k(args-\u003evma) \u0026\u0026 args-\u003eptep)\n\t\tphys |\u003d __pte_to_phys(ptep_get(args-\u003eptep)) \u0026 ~PAGE_MASK_KERNEL;\n\treturn phys;\n```",
